{"step_index":179,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T06:13:18Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. Build a modern, fun, mobile-first web app called:\r\n\r\n🎓 “Student Survival App” 🧑‍🎓🔥\r\n\r\nTagline:\r\n“Survive college. One deadline at a time. 😂”\r\n\r\nThe app should feel like it was made BY students, FOR students — useful, colorful, modern, funny, and slightly chaotic.\r\n\r\nIMPORTANT:\r\n- Make the app fully functional, not just a static UI.\r\n- Make it responsive for mobile, tablet, and laptop.\r\n- Use clean component-based structure.\r\n- Add smooth animations and interactive buttons.\r\n- Use localStorage so user data remains after refreshing.\r\n- No backend is required for the basic version.\r\n- Use realistic sample data on first launch.\r\n- The uploaded image called “Life of a Student” must be used as the main visual identity of the application.\r\n\r\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\r\n🖼️ APP IMAGE / VISUAL IDENTITY\r\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\r\n\r\nUse the uploaded “Life of a Student” image throughout the application.\r\n\r\nThe image shows a notebook-style illustration with the title:\r\n“LIFE OF A STUDENT”\r\n\r\nUse this SAME image in two ways:\r\n\r\n1. APP ICON / LOGO\r\n- Use the uploaded image as the application logo/icon.\r\n- Create a clean circular or rounded-square crop of the image for the logo.\r\n- Show it on the login page.\r\n- Show it in the top navigation/header.\r\n- Use it as the favicon/app icon where technically possible.\r\n- On mobile, use the cropped image as the app icon.\r\n\r\n2. BACKGROUND\r\n- Use the uploaded image as the main background visual.\r\n- Do NOT stretch or distort the image.\r\n- Use it as a full-screen background with:\r\n  background-size: cover;\r\n  background-position: center;\r\n  background-att\n<truncated 12349 bytes>\nApp.<fn> is not a function` error will occur.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Next Steps\n1. **Inspect and Update `app.js` Exports:**\n   - View lines ~2940–2980 of `C:\\Users\\DELL\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\student-survival-app\\app.js`.\n   - Ensure the `return { ... }` block includes:\n     - `switchAuthTab`\n     - `handleSignUp`\n     - `quickDemoLogin`\n     - `openDemoCredentialsModal`\n2. **Synchronize Files:**\n   - Copy all files from `C:\\Users\\DELL\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\student-survival-app` to `C:\\Users\\DELL\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\student survival\\student-survival-app`.\n3. **Smoke Test:**\n   - Launch Edge with `file:///C:/Users/DELL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/student-survival-app/index.html`.\n   - Verify tab switching between \"Sign In\" and \"Create Account\".\n   - Test 1-click login with `aman_sharma` and `rahul_v`.\n   - Test \"Create Account\" submission and verify immediate login.\n4. **Respond to User:** Present the completed feature, credentials table, and launch instructions.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Must retain all existing features: animated splash, glassmorphism cards, 75% attendance math, assignment countdown, canteen status & calculator, weekly timetable, live exam ticker, sleep/study diagnostic, power nap timer, and the sticky notification bar.\n- Do not introduce backend requirements; keep all account registration and session states in browser `localStorage`.\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 3 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790746104770]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/DELL/.gemini/antigravity/brain/b1401ff7-7a8f-4c14-be76-c6f41632d249/.user_uploaded/media_1790746104770.jpg\nLast Edited: 2026-09-30T05:28:28Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: life-of-a-student]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/DELL/.gemini/antigravity/brain/b1401ff7-7a8f-4c14-be76-c6f4163